  {
   "id": 677,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    560,
    300
   ],
   "size": [
    330,
    820
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 10,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "How to use",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## H3 masked edit (inpaint) — Apple Silicon\n\nChange one region of an image and leave the rest untouched.\n\n1. **Source image**: load it, then right-click the node → **Open in MaskEditor** and paint over the area to change. Sides must be multiples of 32 px (most generator outputs are). The example comes pre-masked.\n2. **Reference 1** is the artwork or object to put in (`<Picture 1>`). Do **not** use the source itself as a reference: the model then copies its own mistakes.\n3. **Instruction**: say what `<Picture 1>` supplies, describe what is already in the frame and must stay, then the one thing to add and where.\n4. **Denoise** (Scheduler node): 0.85 corrects lettering and adds props while keeping geometry; 1.0 re-composes the area (needs real content on at least two sides).\n\nThe sampler only changes the masked area; the paste-back puts the render back into the original pixels through a grown (32 px), feathered (24 px) mask, so everything beyond that margin stays pixel-exact.\n\nA ColorTransfer node (core ComfyUI) pulls the render's tone back to the source before the paste; the turbo lane otherwise leaves the masked area a few levels darker. The `h3edit --inpaint` CLI also removes the decoder's faint 16-px grid; this GUI version does not, so a faint grid can show on smooth surfaces. Finish soft areas with the detail pass. Needs ComfyUI-MAINodes (H3V2VInit)."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## H3 masked edit (inpaint) — Apple Silicon\n\nChange one region of an image and leave the rest untouched.\n\n1. **Source image**: load it, then right-click the node → **Open in MaskEditor** and paint over the area to change. Sides must be multiples of 32 px (most generator outputs are). The example comes pre-masked.\n2. **Reference 1** is the artwork or object to put in (`<Picture 1>`). Do **not** use the source itself as a reference: the model then copies its own mistakes.\n3. **Instruction**: say what `<Picture 1>` supplies, describe what is already in the frame and must stay, then the one thing to add and where.\n4. **Denoise** (Scheduler node): 0.85 corrects lettering and adds props while keeping geometry; 1.0 re-composes the area (needs real content on at least two sides).\n\nThe sampler only changes the masked area; the paste-back puts the render back into the original pixels through a grown (32 px), feathered (24 px) mask, so everything beyond that margin stays pixel-exact.\n\nA ColorTransfer node (core ComfyUI) pulls the render's tone back to the source before the paste; the turbo lane otherwise leaves the masked area a few levels darker. The `h3edit --inpaint` CLI also removes the decoder's faint 16-px grid; this GUI version does not, so a faint grid can show on smooth surfaces. Finish soft areas with the detail pass. Needs ComfyUI-MAINodes (H3V2VInit)."
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
